# The bench drills run in Linux containers through the Windows bind mount. A
# CRLF shebang or any `\r`-terminated line breaks bash outright, and autocrlf
# would otherwise hand a Windows checkout CRLF scripts that fail only there —
# the worst kind, since CI on Linux stays green. Pin LF for the things that get
# executed or parsed as bytes.
*.sh                text eol=lf
*.py                text eol=lf
docs/evidence/*.log text eol=lf
